## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design end-to-end Azure OpenAI-powered data-governance tooling that handles multi-tenant isolation, secure KB grounding, and robust testing.

## Key Concepts
- Data lineage ingestion and normalization across Synapse/Data Factory.
- Versioned KB in Azure Blob and Cognitive Search integration.
- Per-tenant isolation with Key Vault-backed Cosmos DB storage.
- Prompt engineering with fallback chains and confidence scoring.
- Data redaction and auditability.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code for gap-filling using KB
async function fillLineageGap(partialLineage, kbClient) {
  if (partialLineage.isComplete()) return partialLineage;
  const kb = await kbClient.query(partialLineage.pattern);
  return partialLineage.enrich(kb);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure the accuracy of enrichment?
- How would you handle cycles or conflicting KB results?

## Why This Is Asked

Probes production-grade multi-tenant routing with cost control, latency targets, RBAC, and integration with Azure services (Cosmos DB, AD, Cognitive Search, Durable Functions, API Management). Assesses ability to design end-to-end data flow, observability, and testing strategies.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant policy and quota management in Cosmos DB
- Multi-model routing: cost-aware model choice + RAG grounding
- Latency budgets and backpressure via Durable Functions
- RBAC via Azure AD and API Management gating
- Grounding via Cognitive Search KB

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal routing decision
function chooseEngine(policies, tenantId, workload) {
  const p = policies[tenantId];
  if (!p) return 'GPT-3.5-turbo';
  if (workload.latencyMs > p.latencyBudget) return p.defaultModel;
  if (workload.costPerRequest > p.costBudget) return 'GPT-3.5-turbo';
  return p.preferredModel;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you model tenant quotas in Cosmos DB for fairness during bursts?
- What tests validate SLA adherence under canary deployments?
- How would you implement backpressure across regional deployments and API gateways?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests real-world infra decisions around data residency, confidential inference, and auditable prompts in a regulated fintech context.

## Key Concepts
- Azure OpenAI in Confidential Computing
- Multi-tenant isolation (RBAC, per-tenant caches)
- Data residency controls and API Management routing
- PII masking and prompt/log redaction
- Audit trails to Data Lake and cost governance

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: redact and route to OpenAI within tenant boundaries
function preparePrompt(input, tenantId){
  const redacted = redactPII(input);
  const region = getTenantRegion(tenantId);
  if(region !== 'allowed-region') throw new Error('Region violation');
  return callOpenAI(redacted, {tenantId});
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate end-to-end latency under peak load?
- What tests would verify region-boundary enforcement and audit completeness?
